 The loop times are at the blank train's 9 tiles per second. The radii are as drawn; the baked spline is a little tighter where a curve meets a straight (`npm run maps` prints the tightest one), and `packages/tools/test/all-maps.test.ts` keeps every map's tightest curve at 17 tiles or more, keeps rock and water off the cars and one side of the track open to ride beside, and checks the track can be reached from the spawn.
 
+### Generated maps
+
+`?map=gen` builds a new 400 × 200 map from the seed instead of loading a file: a loop with S-bends and kidney shapes, mud, rocks, forest, lakes, sandstone mesas, hills, and rivers that cross the track on bridges with shallow fords along them. The same seed gives the same map on every machine, so `?map=gen&seed=outlaw-7` is always the same map. Without `seed` the page picks one; the debug readout (`?debug=on`) shows it.
+
+Each map picks a theme (forest, rocks, mesas, water, mud or balanced) that gets more of that and less of the rest, plus a busyness that makes it a little denser or sparser. The debug readout shows both on its map line, for example `map gen 400x200 (gen:outlaw-7 rocks -0.048)`. Settings are in [Values you can change](#values-you-can-change), and the log and replays keep them, so a replay rebuilds the same map.
+
+Generated maps keep the same rules as the hand-made ones (an open lane on one side, nothing under the cars, curves of 17 tiles or more), and the tests check 300 seeds. `npm run tools -- gen-map <seed>... --out <dir>` checks seeds and writes a layout picture of each.
+
 To make a new map, see [Creating maps](Creating-maps). Map changes (zones, the route, the spawn) are made in Tiled: open the `.tmj` in `packages/content/maps-src/` and save, with `npm run maps:watch` rebuilding the map on every save. A new `.tmj` there becomes a new `?map=` id with no other change. See "Tiled workflow in detail" in the design doc.
 
